From bcdc3c929815542efc969132d1efacc72bf27907 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nanairo8890 <301115931+nanairo8890@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:50:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sm8450-common: load the vendor_dlkm kernel modules at
 early-init

First stage init loads only the vendor_boot ramdisk list. The rest of the
kernel release (display, touch, Wi-Fi, audio, video, camera, data) is in
/vendor_dlkm/lib/modules with the stock load list and blocklist, and
nothing loaded it

Add an own vendor.modprobe service in rootdir/etc/init.vendor_dlkm.rc
that runs the platform /vendor/bin/modprobe -b -s --all=<modules.load> in
AOSP's vendor_modprobe domain at early-init, as stock starts its loader,
and sets vendor.all.modules.ready when it ends:

- --all loads the list in order with its dependencies through
  libmodprobe, like first stage init, and a failing module does not stop
  the others; -b applies the blocklist
- AOSP already allows init to run vendor toolbox as vendor_modprobe and
  vendor_modprobe to load modules from vendor_file, the label of
  /vendor_dlkm, so no new policy is needed
- /vendor_dlkm is mounted in first stage (fstab.qcom)
- the stock Qualcomm vendor_modprobe.sh is not used: it is marked
  confidential and proprietary and does the same with a shell loop

This lifts the vendor.modprobe gate of init-service-qualification.json:
it becomes the one approved vendor service, as an own definition, and
the tests check the service, its domain, its install and the first
stage mount of vendor_dlkm. Not built or tested on hardware
---
 common.mk                         |  5 +++++
 docs/INIT_SERVICE_OWNERSHIP.md    | 10 +++++++---
 init-service-qualification.json   |  9 +++++----
 rootdir/etc/init.vendor_dlkm.rc   | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_init_service_review.py | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 5 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 rootdir/etc/init.vendor_dlkm.rc

